From 2ba23444c892930a439c99d9f26ed499e3996504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 10:37:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0275 -- #1 FIX (real root): null-guard rtl() --
 game.lang NULL before I18N init

THE fix for the organya cold-cache precache crash. Patch 0272's in-LOG fault
handler named it decisively (refuting the OOM hypothesis): it is a SIGSEGV null
deref, not bad_alloc. eip=I18N::isRTL()+0x7 <- Font::getWidth+0x23 <-
_oc_draw_progress+0x1a0 (heap was fine, uordblks ~3.36MB with 250-850KB free).

Root: the rtl() macro (game.h:194) = `game.lang->isRTL()` with no null guard, and
game.lang (I18N*, game.h:70) is new'd at game.cpp:99 -- AFTER the first-launch
organya precache runs. So the precache progress-overlay's text measure
(_oc_draw_progress -> Font::getWidth -> rtl()) dereferences a NULL game.lang.
Benign on DOSBox (null page readable -> precache completes) but a hard SIGSEGV on
g2k/CWSDPMI -- and since it fires in a VESA graphics mode the DJGPP register dump
lands on the unshown text buffer, which is why the operator saw a "silent
quit-to-DOS" across 4 iters. (0273's exception guard can't catch a signal, so it
was ineffective; 0274 moot.)

Fix: `#define rtl() (game.lang ? game.lang->isRTL() : false)`. LTR default when
game.lang is uninitialized (the pre-title overlay text is English/LTR -- correct);
zero behavior change once game.lang is set; fixes ALL early rtl() callers, not
just the precache. The sibling `_(x)` translate macro has the same latent null
deref but is not in the precache path (literal text) so it is left minimal.

Keep 0272 riding for the re-verify (organya cold-cache should now boot THROUGH,
no precache-FAULT line).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/game.h | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game.h b/src/game.h
index 1f03da4d..4ee92e1f 100644
--- a/src/game.h
+++ b/src/game.h
@@ -191,7 +191,20 @@ struct Game
 
 extern Game game;
 #define _(x) game.lang->translate(x)
-#define rtl() game.lang->isRTL()
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0275, #1 FIX): null-guard rtl() -- game.lang (I18N*) is new'd
+// at game.cpp:99 AFTER the organya first-launch precache runs, so the precache's
+// progress-overlay text (_oc_draw_progress -> Font::getWidth/draw -> rtl()) calls
+// rtl() while game.lang is NULL. On g2k/CWSDPMI that null `this` deref is a hard
+// SIGSEGV (confirmed by patch 0272's fault handler: eip=I18N::isRTL()+0x7 <-
+// Font::getWidth+0x23 <- _oc_draw_progress+0x1a0). Benign on DOSBox (null page
+// readable) but fatal on real HW -- the 4-iter "silent quit-to-DOS" root cause
+// (the DJGPP dump landed on the unshown VESA text buffer). LTR default when
+// uninitialized is correct (the pre-title overlay text is English/LTR); no
+// behavior change once game.lang is set. Fixes ALL early rtl() callers, not just
+// the precache. (The sibling `_(x)` translate macro has the same latent null-
+// game.lang deref but is NOT in the precache path -- overlay text is literal,
+// never translated -- so it is left minimal here.)
+#define rtl() (game.lang ? game.lang->isRTL() : false)
 extern TextBox textbox;
 
 extern Object *onscreen_objects[MAX_OBJECTS];
